  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Safe and Responsive Systems in Ghana for Misconduct Reporting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project which is a continuation of GHAB26 seeks to achieve the following outcomes in western and northern regions of Ghana; &#x2022;Support partners to develop safeguarding policies, and safe recruitment practices &#x2022;Support Oxfam and Partners to develop safe programming and safeguarding strategies to ensure programmes are safe &#x2022;Organize safeguarding training and refresher sessions for Safeguarding focal points,  Hold continuous education, and awareness of safeguarding policies and practices among staff of Oxfam, partners and consultants/allies at least every six months, Hold community campaigns including radio to educate and create awareness of the risk of Protection from Sexual Exploitation and Abuse (PSEA) in the development sector, Work with community members and partners to establish reporting mechanisms , Hold training on feminist principles to enable gender transformative approach to safeguarding , Organize discussions on social norms during PSEA community campaigns,</narrative>
  </description>
